Bug fix: peanut pole speed — match server isotropic correction in client prediction.

This commit modifies 2 files (+98/-6 lines), spanning 1 networking, 1 Markdown docs.
This fix addresses a reported bug or regression in the game. Bug fixes in this project follow the TDD protocol: a failing test was written first to reproduce the issue, then the fix was applied to make the test pass, ensuring the defect cannot silently regress.

Additional context from the commit body:
Client prediction used per-axis metric corrections (rNorm*sinPhi floor 0.3) that diverged
from server's isotropic peanutPlayerSpeedCorrection formula at poles (sinPhi→0). This caused
client-server position mismatch → snap-back → perceived sluggishness at poles.

Fix: replace per-axis corrections with server-matching formula:
  speedCorrection = clamp(sqrt(uScale * vScale) / avg, 0.4, 2.5)
Applied isotropically to both predDx and predDy. Average metric lazy-computed once
with same 40-step area-weighted integration as GameRoom.ts _getPeanutAvgMetric.

